 ## Overview
-Swept Volumes via Spacetime Numerical Continuation computes the exact swept volume of a moving shape (brush) by solving for the minimum signed distance function (SDF) over time using numerical continuation, outputting sparse cells representing the spacetime trajectory [S1, unofficial]. It differs from its parent method, SDF Mutation & Eikonal Propagation, by explicitly tracking the temporal argmin of the distance field rather than propagating static distances, and from its sibling, Hierarchical Scalar Field Sculpting, by generating a sparse, trajectory-based representation suitable for dual contouring rather than a dense hierarchical grid [S1, unofficial].
+Swept Volumes via Spacetime Numerical Continuation computes the swept volume of a moving shape (brush) by solving for the minimum signed distance function (SDF) over time using numerical continuation, outputting sparse cells representing the spacetime trajectory [S1, unofficial]. It generates a sparse, trajectory-based representation suitable for dual contouring rather than a dense hierarchical grid [S1, unofficial].
 
